{
  "about": "The sky of Imbar: twelve constellations, one rising in each month of the year of the Sun and Moon (src/campaign/calendar.ts), under which a life is said to be born. Each has its name, the month it rules, a line of what folk who read the sky say of those born under it, its stars, the lines that join them the figure it is named for, and the two gifts (traits of the sign category, data/catalog/traits.json) everyone born under it has (OR-89, OR-117), for a page to draw as a star atlas does. A star is a point on a unit field (x right, y down), its magnitude (1 faint to 4, the sign's brightest, one to a sign) and its colour (0 blue-white to 6 orange, as SkyTexture.stars); a line joins two stars by their order; the figure is an SVG path on a field of 100, its stars set where the creature or thing has its eye, heart and feet. What a sign means in play is the world's to say (see CreationFlow): those who read the sky may read it in you. Orsino's signs were a zodiac animal and an element; Imbar's are its own months.",
